#
# compose/env/local.env.example — operator-tunable variables consumed by
# compose/docker-compose.local.yml (T015, local profile).
#
# Copy to compose/env/local.env (gitignored) and edit. The default values
# below are what `scripts/stargate init` (T016) will write for the local
# profile; for the bring-your-own-env path, copy this file and override.
#
# The local profile is opinionated: the loopback-only DP port (8881), the
# Tor SocksPort/ControlPort (compose-internal only), the UID/GID numerics
# (stargate-cp 5101, stargate-dp 5102, stargate-ipc GID 5100), and the
# named-volume set are NOT operator-tunable — they are the contract the
# rest of the system (T019b/T019c/T022 contract tests, the rendered torrc,
# the inter-plane UDS topology) is wired against. The single operator knob
# this profile exposes is the docker-socket-proxy image digest (Principle
# IV — bump deliberately, never use the bare `:latest` tag).

# docker-socket-proxy image (the only external image this profile pulls —
# Principle IV). Tagged release, not :latest; pinned by multi-arch OCI index
# sha256 digest so amd64/arm64 hosts resolve to the exact tested bytes.
# Digest resolved via `docker buildx imagetools inspect tecnativa/docker-socket-proxy:0.3.0`
# at T015 /start time.
#
# Bump procedure (operator-guidance — the gate now exists):
#   1. Pick a new tagged release (NOT :latest).
#   2. Resolve its multi-arch index digest:
#        docker buildx imagetools inspect tecnativa/docker-socket-proxy:<tag>
#      Use the top-level `Digest:` line (the index digest), not a per-platform
#      manifest digest.
#   3. Update the DOCKER_SOCKET_PROXY_IMAGE line below.
#   4. Confirm the registry still serves that exact digest:
#        STARGATE_GROUND_ONLINE=1 bash scripts/verify.sh
#      The extended scripts/ground-check.sh (section "Compose image pins")
#      now resolves compose `image:` references against the registry in
#      ONLINE mode and FAILs loudly on a pruned/malformed digest. (This
#      closes the gap redteam finding m1 flagged at T015 commit time.)
#   5. The PR-cadence contract test `bash
#      tests/contract/compose/local_compose_test.sh` re-validates the
#      tag@sha256:<64hex> shape on every PR (M9 regex).
DOCKER_SOCKET_PROXY_IMAGE=tecnativa/docker-socket-proxy:0.3.0@sha256:9e4b9e7517a6b660f2cc903a19b257b1852d5b3344794e3ea334ff00ae677ac2
